
## 1. Why Your Posts Aren't Reaching People (The Algorithmic Truth)
X uses strict rules that automatically hold back unverified accounts:

* 
* The Premium Multiplier: X explicitly codes a visibility boost for paying users. Standard X Premium ($8/month) accounts get roughly 6x the reach, and Premium+ gets 15x the reach of free accounts. Without it, your standalone posts are fighting an uphill battle. [1, 3, 4] 
* The External Link Penalty: If you are putting links in your main posts (to a website, store, portfolio, or YouTube video), X is completely suppressing them. For free accounts, posts with external links get near-zero reach because X wants to keep users on its own platform. [2, 5] 
* The "For You" Feed Filter: The main feed defaults to showing content from accounts with high initial engagement or a verification badge. If a brand-new, unverified account simply posts a status update, the algorithm rarely even tests it on an audience. [1, 4, 6] 
